  "status_text": "We just pinned this board down to exactly seven steps. Lean checked both sides on a six-light board where a circuit answers only when one or two lights are on. With one light on, it has to say whether that point has a loop. With two, it says whether the points are joined. One check rules out every circuit of six gates or fewer. The other gives a seven-gate circuit that gets all 21 answers right. Both allow NOT and up to two inputs per gate. Next we test other boards against that seven-gate mark (L-meta-24220, L-meta-40556).",
